OnSite NewBook REST client tests | fake NewBook server built from the public docs (not the real NewBook)

==================== Protocol: URL, auth, envelope, errors, timeouts, retries, rate limit ====================
  PASS  POSTs to <base>/auth_test with HTTP Basic auth and region + api_key in the JSON body
  PASS  success:"true" string envelope is understood and data returned
  PASS  wrong password (HTTP 401) -> AUTH error, not retried
  PASS  wrong api_key (success:"false") -> AUTH error
  PASS  a throttled READ is retried once and succeeds
  PASS  a throttled WRITE is not retried (THROTTLED, outcome known: not applied)
  PASS  a hung READ times out at the read budget (TIMEOUT) and is not retried
  PASS  a hung WRITE times out with outcomeUnknown=true (it may have been applied)
  PASS  HTTP 500 on a write -> SERVER_ERROR, outcomeUnknown=true, sent exactly once
  PASS  HTTP 500 on a read is retried once then reported
  PASS  an unreadable reply to a write -> INVALID_RESPONSE with outcomeUnknown=true
  PASS  client-side limiter stops at max_per_minute without hitting NewBook (100/min limit)
  PASS  credentials (password, api_key) never appear in logs

>>> protocol: PASS (13/13 checks)

==================== Mapping NewBook categories/tariffs/statuses to OnSite sites ====================
  PASS  category -> site: id, name, nightly price from tariff_total / nights
  PASS  capacity, pets, size and amenities are derived from category data
  PASS  a category that does not allow animals is not pet friendly
  PASS  quote sends this party's occupancy (adults, animals) and the category
  PASS  quote returns nights, nightly rate and the NewBook total
  PASS  a fully booked category is marked unavailable; others stay available
  PASS  quote for a category with no free site -> SITE_UNAVAILABLE
  PASS  the cheapest SUCCESSFUL tariff is used (failed tariffs ignored), strings parsed to numbers
  PASS  capacity falls back to adults + children when no combined limit; unknown features are slugged; ft converted to m (largest site)
  PASS  a category with no metadata is never offered (pets/size unknown)
  PASS  category metadata is cached (one accommodation_categories_list call)
  PASS  warm() fills the category cache so the first availability call does not fetch it
  PASS  bestTariff returns null when nothing is bookable
  PASS  statuses map to OnSite statuses
  PASS  names split into first/last; single names get a placeholder surname
  PASS  amenity mapping handles NewBook feature names

>>> mapping: PASS (16/16 checks)

==================== Bookings: create, find, confirm + payment, release ====================
  PASS  bookings_create sends every documented required field (guest name, placeholder address, phone, category, dates)
  PASS  the hold is created as Unconfirmed, with occupancy, and our reference + expiry in the notes
  PASS  result is mapped: id as string, provisional status, NewBook total, account id
  PASS  findBookingByKey finds the booking from our reference in its notes
  PASS  findBookingByKey returns null for an unknown key
  PASS  a second create for the same category/dates when it is full -> SITE_UNAVAILABLE
  PASS  a one-word name is accepted (placeholder surname)
  PASS  getBooking maps an unknown booking to null
  PASS  payment is posted to the booking's client ACCOUNT with our payment id as type_reference, Credit Card type, full amount (not a deposit)
  PASS  booking is then set to Confirmed
  PASS  confirming again does not post the payment twice
  PASS  if the status update fails AFTER the payment was posted, the error surfaces (provider will retry)
  PASS  the retry does NOT double-post the payment and finishes the confirmation
  PASS  a part-payment is flagged as a deposit
  PASS  confirming a CANCELLED booking is refused (BOOKING_RELEASED) and posts no payment
  PASS  release cancels an unpaid hold with the configured cancellation reason id (looked up by name)
  PASS  release does not send notes (they could overwrite our reference)
  PASS  release NEVER cancels a booking that is no longer a hold (confirmed stays confirmed)
  PASS  releasing an unknown booking -> NOT_FOUND
  PASS  a cancellation reason name that does not exist -> CONFIG error (and the booking is left alone)
  PASS  an unknown payment type name -> CONFIG error, nothing posted, booking not confirmed

